# Libraries that must NOT be shipped inside the AppImage.
#
# Vendored from https://github.com/AppImage/pkg2appimage/blob/master/excludelist
# (snapshot taken 2026-10-25), restricted to the two categories this project
# cares about, with deliberate local deviations documented inline.
#
# Format: one file name per line (matched against the SONAME / DT_NEEDED name).
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored. Glob patterns for
# driver/vendor libraries live in `is_excluded()` in bundle.sh and are
# documented there.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. glibc and its loader. A bundled libc cannot work: the dynamic loader,
#    NSS modules, locale/gconv data and the kernel-facing bits all have to match
#    the running system, and the AppImage's whole point is to run on a *newer*
#    glibc than it was built against (see verify.sh, which enforces the 2.35
#    floor this file implies).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ld-linux.so.2
ld-linux-x86-64.so.2
ld-linux-aarch64.so.1
ld-linux-armhf.so.3
ld64.so.2
libanl.so.1
libBrokenLocale.so.1
libc.so.6
libcidn.so.1
libcrypt.so.1
libdl.so.2
libm.so.6
libmvec.so.1
libnsl.so.1
libnss_compat.so.2
libnss_db.so.2
libnss_dns.so.2
libnss_files.so.2
libnss_hesiod.so.2
libnss_nis.so.2
libnss_nisplus.so.2
libpthread.so.0
libresolv.so.2
librt.so.1
libthread_db.so.1
libutil.so.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Graphics stack / GPU drivers. These are loaded against the *host* kernel
#    driver and the host's DRI/ICD configuration; a bundled copy either fails
#    to load or renders nothing. wgpu reaches Vulkan through dlopen anyway, so
#    none of this is a DT_NEEDED of the app (libmpv's own GL/Vulkan output is
#    compiled out).
#
#    Note what is deliberately NOT here:
#      * libva.so.2 and libva-x11/wayland ARE bundled (they are the API library,
#        a hard DT_NEEDED of libmpv once -Dvaapi is on; the vendor driver they
#        dlopen stays on the host),
#      * libX11/libxcb/libwayland-client are bundled too so the app never
#        depends on the host having them at a compatible version,
#      * **libdrm.so.2 is bundled**, although upstream lists it: it is a stable
#        userspace ioctl wrapper, not a driver, and it is a hard NEEDED of
#        libva-x11/libva-wayland, which libmpv links. Leaving it out made the
#        whole AppImage refuse to start on a system without it
#        (`error while loading shared libraries: libdrm.so.2`) -- measured, not
#        assumed. The driver-only siblings (libdrm_amdgpu/intel/radeon/nouveau)
#        stay excluded,
#      * libstdc++.so.6 is bundled because libplacebo (mpv's mandatory
#        dependency) is C++; the alternative was another hard host dependency.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
libGL.so.1
libEGL.so.1
libGLX.so.0
libGLdispatch.so.0
libOpenGL.so.0
libglapi.so.0
# libdrm.so.2 itself is bundled on purpose (see the note above); only the
# driver-facing parts of libdrm are excluded.
libdrm_amdgpu.so.1
libdrm_intel.so.1
libdrm_nouveau.so.2
libdrm_radeon.so.1
libgbm.so.1
libvulkan.so.1
libvulkan_lvp.so
